# QA M6 regression (was qa_m6_bug_zaunerstollen_rolls_off_b2; fixed by
# D-102, E42): Bad Ischl's Zaunerstollen must stay on balcony B2 (the
# Strobl balcony bug of the D-097 addendum item 2, again). QA's relaxed-run
# prefix (walking; the Mozartkugel at the start, Zuckerschock from 350) up
# onto B2 (cols 232-237, row 11) at 3442, then she steps under the Z-box
# (235, row 8), bumps it with a standing hop (3461) and stands still on the
# balcony. The bug: the Zaunerstollen rose onto the box top, rolled right,
# dropped onto the 1-high flower box at 237 (row 10), rolled off it and
# off the balcony and was lost. Since D-102 (E42 addendum) a stone end
# pier (237, rows 7-10) one tile above the box top, joined to the box by a
# stone bridge at (236, row 8), stops it: it turns at the pier's face, rolls
# back left off the box and into her on the balcony.
# Re-cut for D-102 (E42): the relaxed run's braking after the notch-2 leap
# is shifted for the kerb at 151 (2405-2440, rest at the same x), as in
# qa_m6_bad_ischl_relaxed; from 2441 on everything is as before.
# Expected (as in Strobl since its 3-high stopper): the 1-up comes back to
# her on the balcony (ExtraLife, lives 4).
level  = bad_ischl
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Hurt event=PowerUp event=ExtraLife lives=4 player_y<=146
